## Start

```bash
uv sync
uv run pre-commit install
```

`uv sync` installs Python 3.13 if it is missing, creates `.venv` and writes `uv.lock`. Commit `uv.lock`.

## Checks

```bash
uv run pre-commit run --all-files
uv run pytest
```

Pre-commit only checks files git knows about, so `git add` new files first.

## Where things are

- `AGENTS.md` and `.claude/rules/`: how the code is laid out and written
- `decisions.md`: the setup decisions, the lint rules and this project's own decisions

